                <h2 style="font-size:24px;font-weight:800;color:var(--md-heading);margin:0 0 18px;letter-spacing:-0.3px;">Why quick commerce clones don't really exist</h2>
                <p>The 'Blinkit clone' market is mostly grocery delivery templates rebranded as quick commerce. The fundamental problem: <strong>quick commerce isn't a UI &mdash; it's a unit economics + operations engine</strong>. Specifically:</p><ul><li><strong>Dark store geofencing</strong> &mdash; route order to nearest store with stock, in &lt;30 seconds</li><li><strong>Picker dispatch within 60 seconds</strong> &mdash; or the 10-min promise dies</li><li><strong>ETA accuracy modelling</strong> &mdash; predict + display real ETA, not optimistic</li><li><strong>Stock-out + substitution logic</strong> &mdash; happens on 8&ndash;15% of orders</li><li><strong>Unit economics tracking</strong> &mdash; AOV, picker efficiency, last-mile cost &mdash; or you bleed money invisibly</li></ul><p>None of these come in a clone template. They require custom engineering with deep operational understanding.</p>
